WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.954
The fourth job is connecting your team to the rest of Vanderbilt.

2
00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:10.905
Your team needs things it does not control: approvals, information, help from other offices,

3
00:00:10.955 --> 00:00:13.880
and a fair hearing when someone asks too much.

4
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:19.055
New managers do this job least, because nobody told them it was part of the job.

5
00:00:19.105 --> 00:00:19.895
Three habits.

6
00:00:19.945 --> 00:00:26.364
Know the people your team depends on: your HCM, your Engagement Consultant, Finance, a peer manager.

7
00:00:26.414 --> 00:00:32.379
By name, before you need them. Watch for what is coming, so the team hears it from you first.

8
00:00:32.429 --> 00:00:38.653
Speak up for your team: facts, options, and a negotiated date, before you say yes to the weekend.

9
00:00:38.703 --> 00:00:45.768
For example: the week before Commencement, Events asks a Student Affairs manager for her whole team on Friday.

10
00:00:45.818 --> 00:00:48.937
She already knows the events coordinator by name.

11
00:00:48.987 --> 00:00:51.977
The schedule was on her wall calendar in March.

12
00:00:52.027 --> 00:00:57.346
Over coffee, with the printed hours, she names the conflict and offers two options.

13
00:00:57.396 --> 00:01:04.396
He picks one, nobody works the weekend, and on Commencement morning the welcome tables are staffed and ready.

14
00:01:04.446 --> 00:01:08.277
This week: have coffee with one person your team depends on.

